# Adding Z to the permits list of dep's sealed interface S changes no member of S, only its
# PermittedSubclasses attribute. It still changes what compiles against S: an exhaustive
# `switch (s) { case X x -> ...; case Y y -> ...; }` stops compiling. So the change must reach S's
# API hash, or dependents of S are not recompiled. Cross-module, so the external-API path is
# checked.
# `use` only refers to S, in Java 17 syntax, because pattern matching in switch needs Java 21 and
# this test runs on JDK 17 too. For a Java dependent, being recompiled is the whole question:
# javac then reports the non-exhaustive switch itself.
> use/compile
$ sleep 2000
$ copy-file changes/S.java dep/src/main/java/S.java
$ copy-file changes/Z.java dep/src/main/java/Z.java
> use/checkRecompilations 1 A
